e how  precarious that makes my situation  glenn meets his end after daryl punches  negan prompting the villain to randomly  select glenn to murder  the moment is violent and gruesome as  glenn chokes out his last words to his  wife who can't  bear the sight of his grotesquely beaten  visage  the characters and audience watch  helplessly as a character who's been  around a whole lot longer than most  is brought to a bitter bloody end while  the show's worst deaths peel hollow  glen's death is heavy with actual  meaning  negan is not an easily solvable problem  and thus  his death is not there to distract from  this fact as  so many lesser deaths are in the wake of  his death it once again feels like  no one is truly safe unlike other deaths  glenn's demise isn't signaled with  shoehorned dialogue or a sudden  significant moment of calm  he dies at the height of his life with a  new safe haven to call home and a wife  who's about to give birth to their first  child this moment sends a clear message  that the show  will never be the same  people you love  they made you who you are they're still  part of you  the reason that jesus's death remains  one of the walking dead's worst  character endings has a lot to do with  the fact that his comic  book counterpart is so much better on  the page  jesus is a capable fighter and as actor  tom payne noted in an interview with the  hollywood reporter he spent all his time  training for fight scenes that never  actually came  jesus is a big part of the war against  the saviors in the comics his death is  supposed to draw audiences  into a scary new plot featuring a  powerful threat but  all it does is disappoint in what ends  up being the only scene showing what  fans wanted from jesus  he uses his sword to take down multiple  walkers in one of the most well done  action sequences on the show then it all  ends with him taking a swipe at a walker  only to discover the walker is actually  a member of the newly discovered  whisperer faction  wearing a disguise while this is a cool  way to introduce a villain  it's a lame ending for a character who  should have been the coolest thing to  hit the walking dead since the arrival  of negan  no matter what they've done they're  people  there's many kinds of danger many kinds  of dying  no ending on the walking dead embodies  the series blend of tension  horror and emotion more than moral  dixons after making a splash in just  two episodes of the show back in season  one merle comes back in a big way in  season three as one of the governor's  right-hand men  however once his baby brother daryl is  back in the equation  it becomes clear that merle does in fact  have an odd sense of loyalty  eventually he chooses daryl over the  governor but is frustrated to find that  his little bro  isn't interested in choosing him over  rick in an effort to prove that he's the  only one with the guts to do what's  necessary in this new world  merle goes rogue and takes his very own  shot at the governor  unfortunately it doesn't work out though  merle manages to take out a large number  of the villain's men  he's quickly overwhelmed killed and left  to turn  this brings an end to his character arc  and brutally proves that he was wrong  all along daryl finds his undead brother  and puts him down in a cathartic display  of anger  showing that the dixon brothers are by  far the most complicated characters on  the show  you need to grow up things different now  one glaring issue with abraham's death  is that it's  shamelessly milked as a cliffhanger  season six concludes with negan's  infamous introduction  an agonizing six months of speculation  among fans followed  at last the show returned and it was  revealed that the biggest guy in the  group who  isn't main character rick grimes is the  one negan decides to take off the board  seeing a member of the group who is so  tough and has survived so much be  violently killed while his friends are  helpless to do anything about it  is hard to stomach however all that  tension and purpose gets thrown out the  window  when in the season seven premiere negan  murders glenn in the exact same way  glenn had been around since the second  episode of the series he has a wife  pregnant with her first child who is  forced to watch as he is unceremoniously  beaten to death  glenn's death might very well be the  most gut-wrenching demise on an  already bloody show abraham should not  have shared the spotlight with him at  that pivotal moment  despite the character arc that this  death at negan's hands brings to a close  he'll forever be remembered as the guy  who dies before glenn  while some of the best character endings  come as the result of an impactful story  coming to a worthwhile close  others make the list simply because it's  fun to see an incredibly evil character  go down  for two long seasons beta acts as a  leader of the whisperers while carrying  out  ruthless attacks although he pays  deferrings to alpha and follows her with  almost dog-like loyalty  her death does not put a stop to his  wicked ways he carries out her legacy by  unleashing a horde of zombies  on some of the only remaining  non-whisperer human beings in the area  after making life a living hell for our  heroes for several years  beta finally bites off more than he can  chew when he leads his horde against  daryl and negan  after losing what's left of his mind at  the sight of negan the man who killed  alpha  beta throws a walker on him before  slamming him onto the ground  several times just when it looks like  it's lights out for negan  daryl swoops in and jams two knives into  beta's eyes  he is then killed by the very walkers  who gave him protection all these awful  years  if that's not a satisfying end to a  villain we don't know what  is ending on the show it is important to  note that his ending hasn't  actually happened yet but he's off the  franchise temporarily  the season 9 episode what comes after  serves as an  hour-long goodbye to the walking dead's  main character unfortunately  it doesn't make a ton of sense in his  ongoing effort to unite the groups he  now leads after the war with negan  rick is wounded while desperately trying  to lead a herd away from the living  bleeding out and driven only by his  desire to save the people he loves he  continues to lure walker's way  as he hallucinates some of the most  emotional moments of his life  curiously absent from his poignant  hallucinations however  are his recently deceased son his very  much alive daughter  and his long deceased wife laurie those  odd absences aren't the only weird  things about the episode  the entire episode plays out like a  colossal victory lap for the character  but it's unclear exactly what the  victory is  his people are far from safe in fact  they're more divided and in need of  leadership than ever  his son has recently died in the war  whose fallout he is still trying to fix  despite the heroes ending he gets by  blowing up a bridge of walkers  rick doesn't exactly leave the series on  a high note  it's a triumphal exit the show simply  doesn't earn  i'm not the good guy anymore  when sasha first arrives in season 3 the  show spends a lot of time not quite  knowing what to do with her her life  takes a major turn when she begins to  develop feelings for abraham  unfortunately their romance is cut short  by abraham's death  similar to maggie sasha spends what is  left of her life enmeshed in the war  with the saviors  seeking revenge unlike maggie sasha  isn't pregnant and is thus able to  really inflict some damage  she and rosita embark on an  assassination mission  before they're separated sasha pays  tribute to her late love interest by  remarking that negan denied him the  honor of going out fighting  sadly her assassination attempt fails  off-screen  she's captured and negan makes it clear  that he plans to use her to get  alexandria to surrender  locked in a cell disarmed and having had  all hope removed  sasha still manages to hatch a pretty  stellar plan  she convinces eugene to give her a  suicide pill so that when negan makes  his big reveal of having taken her as a  prisoner she can attack him as a walker  in front of all of alexandria  although she fails to exact the revenge  she sought  she still manages to honor abraham by  going out fighting  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the walking dead are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

